' outputs are tied together. The formal A-FDT setup treats the other copy's node as separate, so defection still looks dominant, and I'm sticking with that reading.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm checking whether the two copies' nodes are logically linked by symmetry, since under an interventionist model intervening on my node would leave the other copy's output at its prior, which would make defection look dominant like in CDT.\n\nI'm going back over whether the two copies' outputs are tied together. The formal A-FDT setup treats the other copy's node as separate, so defection still looks dominant, and I'm sticking with that reading.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9959,"completion_tokens":732,"total_tokens":10691,"cost":0.054476,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.054476,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.039836,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01464},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":247,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}